{"In fetch_error_details(), error_ids are paired with nodestore results via zip(error_ids, events.values()), but nodestore.get_multi() can return a dict whose iteration order does not match the input IDs. This can attach the wrong title/message/timestamp to a given error_id, producing incorrect replay summaries.": 0.9384210705757141, "When the 'use-table-widget-visualization' feature is enabled, WidgetCardChart renders TableWidgetVisualization with empty columns and empty tableData, ignoring actual query results. This makes table widgets render blank for any org with that feature flag.": 0.9964463114738464, "BrowserReportSerializer.validate_timestamp/validate_age uses truthiness checks on initial_data.get('age') and initial_data.get('timestamp'), so age=0 and timestamp=0 can bypass the mutual-exclusion validation and allow both fields simultaneously. This accepts structurally invalid reports per the serializer's own intended constraints.": 0.9320966601371765}